{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #18: declared status 'open'. Formalized: yes. We call $m$ practical if every integer $n<m$ is the sum of distinct divisors of $m$. If $m$ is practical then let $h(m)$  be such that $h(m)$ many divisors always suffice.\n\nAre there infinitely many practical $m$ such that\\[h(m) < (\\log\\log m)^{O(1)}?\\]Is it true that $h(n!)<n^{o(1)}$? Or perhaps even $h(n!)<(\\log n)^{O(1)}$? Prize: no. OEIS: A005153. Tags: divisors, factorials, number theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_2e262c1fe8a9dc5d5d53ea6f96220b68faac8b0b75c581a7c98d858901250b15","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:18","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_ea911c7b75a654e8","object_root":"sha256:429db107c1171e4a89abd7c827d78744015e6e9ea24cc01fe119b90da52634f9","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:18"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"vela.claim-record.v1"}